# Fault J-A-2: a balance resting on a move with a window day and a hole amount printed only the window's question,
# not the amount's. L §8.1: a hole "prints every question it carries, sorted by code point and without duplicates".
# The January card spending is a hole on a day within January: the balance on 2026-01-14 carries both questions (q).
# (The fault's text stated `outside DUK`; an outside place states no unit now (L §5.10), so it is dropped here.)
# tally 2.2.1 R21 (L §8.2 `unknown day:`): the name is the cell a caller pins, `added <entry> of <calendar>`, else
# the movement; tally 2.2 printed the window's text or `added <entry>`.
# tally 2.3 (G1, #247): a window that reaches a move's `on` or `at` makes it a hole day (L §4.4 A movement takes a
# day, §5.14): the movement's places are the hole on every day, HOLE-IMPRECISE naming the day; re-stored.
# tally 2.3 (the households' speed, #247): re-stored again: a hole-day balance names its day's question and
# reads, as tally 2.2.1's `?` day did; W1's additions (a hole amount's questions, the reads past a reading) went.
=== m.tally
model f
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
source s "synthetic"
place konto: accounts DUK lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input spend[m in months]: money DUK
move cards[m in months]: transfers
  on window(start_of(m), end_of(m) - 1 day)
  leg cash from konto to world amount spend[m]
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 0 at 2026-01-01 start
  spend[*] = ?"card spending"
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-14)
=== expect
q: ?"date within window(2026-01-01, 2026-01-31) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-01]" (cards[2026-01]) ?"date within window(2026-02-01, 2026-02-28) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-02]" (cards[2026-02]) ?"date within window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-31) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-03]" (cards[2026-03]) ?"date within window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-30) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-04]" (cards[2026-04]) ?"date within window(2026-05-01, 2026-05-31) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-05]" (cards[2026-05]) ?"date within window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-30) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-06]" (cards[2026-06]) ?"date within window(2026-07-01, 2026-07-31) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-07]" (cards[2026-07]) ?"date within window(2026-08-01, 2026-08-31) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-08]" (cards[2026-08]) ?"date within window(2026-09-01, 2026-09-30) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-09]" (cards[2026-09]) ?"date within window(2026-10-01, 2026-10-31) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-10]" (cards[2026-10]) ?"date within window(2026-11-01, 2026-11-30) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-11]" (cards[2026-11]) ?"date within window(2026-12-01, 2026-12-31) not precise enough for the day of cards[2026-12]" (cards[2026-12])
  unknown day: cards[2026-01]
  unknown day: cards[2026-02]
  unknown day: cards[2026-03]
  unknown day: cards[2026-04]
  unknown day: cards[2026-05]
  unknown day: cards[2026-06]
  unknown day: cards[2026-07]
  unknown day: cards[2026-08]
  unknown day: cards[2026-09]
  unknown day: cards[2026-10]
  unknown day: cards[2026-11]
  unknown day: cards[2026-12]
  cut 2026-01-01
